</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Ambulance organisations misreported 999 response times</article-title><source>Guardian Unlimited</source><year>2006</year><comment>Aug. 15th. Available from <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.guardian.co.uk/uk_news/story/0,,1844679,00.html">http://www.guardian.co.uk/uk_news/story/0,,1844679,00.html</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="b31"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chassin</surname><given-names>MR</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Achieving and sustaining improved quality: lessons from New York State and cardiac surgery</article-title><source>Hlth Aff.</source><year>2002</year><volume>21</volume><fpage>40</fpage><lpage>51</lpage><comment>no. 4</comment></citation></ref><ref id="b32"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Clinical Resource and Audit Group</collab><source>Clinical Outcome Indicators: a Report from the Clinical Outcomes Working Group</source><year>2002</year><publisher-loc>Edinburgh</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Scottish Executive</publisher-name><comment>Available from <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="http://www.show.scot.nhs.uk/crag">http://www.show.scot.nhs.uk/crag</ext-link></comment></citation></ref><ref id="b33"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Codman</surname><given-names>EA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Uniformity in hospital morbidity reports</article-title><source>Bost. Med. Surg. J.</source><year>1917</year><volume>177</volume><fpage>279</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="b34"><citation citation-type="book"><collab>Commission for Health Improvement</collab><source>NHS Performance Ratings: Acute Organisations, Specialist Organisations, Ambulance Organisations 2002/03</source><year>2003a</year><publisher-loc>London</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Stationery Office</publisher-name><c